{!$Input:Document.Id}
You have received one or more Job Description documents from {!$RelatedList:Document.CombinedAttachments.Records}.
TASKS 1. Parse each Job Description and output one JSON object per file. 2. Use the exact schema below. 3. Fill missing data as an empty string "" (do not use null, unknown, or omit the field). 4. Preserve the exact spelling and formatting from the JD for all text fields. 5. Ensure "ar", "experience", and "opportunityAmount" contain only numeric values (no words like "years" or "months"). 6. Dates must be in YYYY-MM-DD format. 7. Do not add newlines inside string values; keep each value on one line. 8. Output **must be ONLY the JSON object** — no code fences, no extra text, no commentary.
SCHEMA { "jobs": [ { "jobDescription": { "title": "", "ar": "", // numeric only "companyName": "", "experience": "", // numeric only "tagline": "", "responsibilities": "", "otherLocation": "", "preferredLocation": "", "qualifications": "", "seniority": "", "skillsRequired": "", "source": "", "opportunityName": "", "opportunityCloseDate": "", // YYYY-MM-DD "opportunityAmount": "" // numeric only } } ] }
STRICT RULES - No commentary or text outside the JSON braces. - No ``` or other code fences. - No null or "unknown" values; use "" if missing. - Keep numeric fields numeric only (e.g., "5" not "5 years"). - Keep all string values on a single line (no embedded line breaks).

